{"id":"sling","name":"Sling","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:sling"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Sling","text":"With a sling and a stone David smote the Philistine giant (1 Sam. 17:40, 49). There were 700 Benjamites who were so skilled in its use that with the left hand they “could sling stones at a hair breadth, and not miss” (Judg. 20:16; 1 Chr. 12:2). It was used by the Israelites in war (2 Kings 3:25). (See ARMS.) The words in Prov. 26:8, “As he that bindeth a stone in a sling,” etc. (Authorized Version), should rather, as in the Revised Version, be “As a bag of gems in a heap of stones,” etc."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","xlit":"Pᵉlishtîy","gloss":"a Pelishtite or inhabitant of Pelesheth","kjv":"Philistine","count":10,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H68","lemma":"אֶבֶן","xlit":"ʼeben","gloss":"a stone","kjv":"carbuncle, mason, plummet, stone","count":7,"share":0.47},{"strong":"H7050","lemma":"קֶלַע","xlit":"qelaʻ","gloss":"a sling","kjv":"hanging, leaf, sling","count":3,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H7049","lemma":"קָלַע","xlit":"qâlaʻ","gloss":"to sling","kjv":"carve, sling","count":2,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H4731","lemma":"מַקֵּל","xlit":"maqqêl","gloss":"a shoot","kjv":"rod, staff","count":2,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H4634","lemma":"מַעֲרָכָה","xlit":"maʻărâkâh","gloss":"an arrangement","kjv":"army, fight, be set in order, ordered place","count":2,"share":0.13}],"verses":["1Sam.17.40","1Sam.17.41","1Sam.17.42","1Sam.17.43","1Sam.17.44","1Sam.17.45","1Sam.17.46","1Sam.17.48","1Sam.17.49","1Sam.17.50","Judg.20.16","1Sam.17.47","2Kgs.3.25","2Chr.26.14","Prov.26.8"],"related":[{"id":"armies","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"arms","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"championship","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.123,"why":"8 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"courage","type":"cooccur","shared":11,"jaccard":0